🚑 Technology Meets Compassion: Improving Emergency Care Through Innovation.
Emergency care is not only about how quickly patients receive treatment, but also how effectively healthcare professionals communicate, coordinate, and 
work together to save lives. This project, “Improving Emergency Room Referral and Patient Transfer in the Philippines Through a Digital Referral System,” 
highlights the challenges of emergency referrals, including delayed communication, incomplete documentation, and difficulties coordinating patient transfers 
between healthcare facilities. Through the proposed Digital Emergency Referral and Patient Transfer System (DERPTS), 
I aim to emphasize how technology can help create a more organized, efficient, and coordinated referral process through standardized documentation,
real-time communication, referral tracking, and timely notifications. As a future registered nurse, I recognize that providing quality 
healthcare goes beyond bedside care. It also involves embracing innovation, 
strengthening teamwork, and finding better ways to ensure patient safety and continuity of care.
Because in emergency situations, every second matters, every communication counts, and every patient deserves timely care.
Innovation should never replace compassion; it should make compassionate care better. 💙
